# reference PPO+CTLE implementation. Not ours to redistribute, and a binary
# blob besides. Kept on disk, out of history. Read it before Task 2; do not
# anchor on its numbers (same standing rule as ams_rl_ppo, CLAUDEwa §4.2).
PCI.2/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PDK — SKY130.
#
# The working install lives OUT OF TREE at C:\Users\DELL\sky130A (HANDOFF G33),
# so nothing here should match today. These patterns exist so that a PDK copied
# or symlinked into the repo (~52 MB, 856 files, and not ours to redistribute)
# cannot be committed by accident.
#
# NOT ignored, and must stay tracked:
#   nebula/device/spice/sky130_nfet_only.lib.spice  — OUR trimmed library (G36).
#   It contains only `.include` pointers into the out-of-tree PDK plus a header
#   and `.option scale=1.0u`; it redistributes no model cards.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
sky130A/
sky130_fd_pr/
sky130*/
libs.tech/
libs.ref/
open_pdks/
volare/
*.pm3.spice
*.corner.spice
!nebula/device/spice/sky130_nfet_only.lib.spice
# ... and its passive-carrying successor (task 4c). Same argument: 735 lines of
# `.include` pointers plus `.option scale=1.0u`, redistributing no model cards.
# 25 (MOS x passive) corner sections; see HANDOFF G58.
!nebula/device/spice/sky130_ctle.lib.spice

